y><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Trucking Rejection Rates: Why Holiday Shipping Gets SPICY</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucking-rejection-rates-why-holiday-shipping-gets-spicy-b435c10f48/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucking-rejection-rates-why-holiday-shipping-gets-spicy-b435c10f48/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:30:03 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Q3 Shipping Costs Down 3.3% – Where Did The Savings Go?</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/q3-shipping-costs-down-3-3-where-did-the-savings-go-4300ecbcef/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/q3-shipping-costs-down-3-3-where-did-the-savings-go-4300ecbcef/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:29:13 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Trucking groups press Congress for lame-duck action</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucking-groups-press-congress-for-lame-duck-action-f71e73d196/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucking-groups-press-congress-for-lame-duck-action-f71e73d196/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:59:42 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Transport Topics</description></item><item><title>Truckers face 20-hour wait crossing the Tocantins River on BR-235 as bridge closure and limited ferry service affect corn shipment</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truckers-face-20-hour-wait-crossing-the-tocantins-river-on-br-235-as-b-d4cd4a413f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truckers-face-20-hour-wait-crossing-the-tocantins-river-on-br-235-as-b-d4cd4a413f/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:56:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>CPG Click Oil and Gas</description></item><item><title>13 suspects charged in $22M freight train cargo theft scheme in US</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/13-suspects-charged-in-22m-freight-train-cargo-theft-scheme-in-us-e0a2d5aa87/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/13-suspects-charged-in-22m-freight-train-cargo-theft-scheme-in-us-e0a2d5aa87/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:52:14 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Thirteen men were charged Thursday over an alleged freight train theft operation that prosecutors say took more than $22 million in cargo bound for major retailers. A federal indictment unsealed the same day says the suspects targeted more than 36 trains carrying Nike sneakers, Crocs footwear and power tools that came through the ports of Los Angeles and Long Beach. Prosecutors allege the group disabled trains by damaging their braking systems at set locations, then moved the goods onto trucks. The merchandise was sold to an unidentified company that allegedly resold it. First Assistant US Attorney Bill Essayli called the alleged thefts &quot;staggering&quot; and promised further prosecutions in similar cases. All 13 defendants face conspiracy and theft of interstate railroad cargo charges, and two of them also face a count involving violence against railroad carriers. If convicted, they could face federal prison terms of five to 20 years.</description></item><item><title>Mexico tightens trucking oversight with new digital compliance rules</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/mexico-tightens-trucking-oversight-with-new-digital-compliance-rules-6eaf6190f3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/mexico-tightens-trucking-oversight-with-new-digital-compliance-rules-6eaf6190f3/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:37:12 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Zim Q3 profit surges to $830 million as freight rates jump 55%</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/zim-q3-profit-surges-to-830-million-as-freight-rates-jump-55-b1d1840b89/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/zim-q3-profit-surges-to-830-million-as-freight-rates-jump-55-b1d1840b89/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:26:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>At least 36 Southern California trains burglarised in $22.5 million cargo theft racket; 14 accused allege</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/at-least-36-southern-california-trains-burglarised-in-22-5-million-car-50b1547c4e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/at-least-36-southern-california-trains-burglarised-in-22-5-million-car-50b1547c4e/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:18:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The US Department of Justice said 14 people have been indicted over alleged thefts of more than $22.5 million in cargo from freight trains in Southern California. According to the DOJ, the group burglarised at least three dozen trains between February 2024 and August 2026, taking goods that included Nike sneakers and Milwaukee tools. Investigators allege members cut air hoses to force emergency stops, then boarded the trains and removed valuable cargo.

Thirteen of the 14 defendants were arrested on Thursday, and the case is a 17-count federal indictment. Investigators allege two defendants sold thousands of pairs of stolen Nike sneakers to a Los Angeles resale business, receiving approximately $1,081,493 between May and October 2025. The alleged leader is identified as Nathan Daniel Angel, 21, of East Los Angeles. All defendants are presumed innocent unless proven guilty in court.</description></item><item><title>Freight Broker Blames Injured Emlenton Mechanic, Seeks to Add Disabled Truck Owner to I-80 Lawsuit</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/freight-broker-blames-injured-emlenton-mechanic-seeks-to-add-disabled-72fe5a4205/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/freight-broker-blames-injured-emlenton-mechanic-seeks-to-add-disabled-72fe5a4205/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:12:09 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>exploreVenango</description></item><item><title>Union Pacific–Norfolk Southern Merger Draws Labor Support, Shipper Concerns</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/union-pacific-norfolk-southern-merger-draws-labor-support-shipper-conc-7db84ccb46/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/union-pacific-norfolk-southern-merger-draws-labor-support-shipper-conc-7db84ccb46/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:10:31 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Good Carriers, Wrong Drivers: Why Cargo Theft Is Moving Past Carrier Vetting</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/good-carriers-wrong-drivers-why-cargo-theft-is-moving-past-carrier-vet-7de5f0a5c0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/good-carriers-wrong-drivers-why-cargo-theft-is-moving-past-carrier-vet-7de5f0a5c0/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>ATA names five finalists for 2026 National Driver of the Year award</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/ata-names-five-finalists-for-2026-national-driver-of-the-year-award-9f32659279/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/ata-names-five-finalists-for-2026-national-driver-of-the-year-award-9f32659279/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:50:49 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>BlueGrace Logistics secures Littlejohn as new private equity partner</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/bluegrace-logistics-secures-littlejohn-as-new-private-equity-partner-1788d3d0db/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/bluegrace-logistics-secures-littlejohn-as-new-private-equity-partner-1788d3d0db/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:37:46 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Dallas College, Goodwill Expand CDL Training Program</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/dallas-college-goodwill-expand-cdl-training-program-bcf2256ac9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/dallas-college-goodwill-expand-cdl-training-program-bcf2256ac9/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:24:44 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Dallas College and Goodwill Dallas have teamed up with FleetForce Truck Driver Training to widen CDL instruction across Dallas-Fort Worth. The program covers Class A, B and C licenses and combines classroom work with hands-on training, with FleetForce instructors teaching at Goodwill facilities. The Dallas location is FleetForce&#x27;s 17th in the U.S. The company&#x27;s Next10,000 campaign aims to train 10,000 students through 2026 and cites about 6,100 local CDL openings in the region. Qualified graduates are guaranteed an interview with a large full-truckload carrier through FleetForce&#x27;s Pre-Hire network. The article does not yet give enrollment figures or completion and placement rates for Dallas students.</description></item><item><title>Truckload freight keeps shifting toward LTL as rates rise in both sectors</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truckload-freight-keeps-shifting-toward-ltl-as-rates-rise-in-both-sect-a4a0fcdf29/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truckload-freight-keeps-shifting-toward-ltl-as-rates-rise-in-both-sect-a4a0fcdf29/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:06:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Journal of Commerce</description></item><item><title>Trucker sentenced in $7.2 million cargo theft scheme involving legitimate freight contracts</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-sentenced-in-7-2-million-cargo-theft-scheme-involving-legitima-50baa1f41e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-sentenced-in-7-2-million-cargo-theft-scheme-involving-legitima-50baa1f41e/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:00:48 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Transport truck driver charged after rollerblader struck and killed in Ajax: police</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/transport-truck-driver-charged-after-rollerblader-struck-and-killed-in-c26984b5d7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/transport-truck-driver-charged-after-rollerblader-struck-and-killed-in-c26984b5d7/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:34:50 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>CTV News</description></item><item><title>TCA&#x27;s Heller: Enforcement crackdown reshaping US trucking, but FMCSA needs more resources</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/tca-s-heller-enforcement-crackdown-reshaping-us-trucking-but-fmcsa-nee-aaf6ac14ad/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/tca-s-heller-enforcement-crackdown-reshaping-us-trucking-but-fmcsa-nee-aaf6ac14ad/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:30:42 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><descriptio