ints to an October 2026 Transport Topics examination that described companies including Descartes and Highway connecting identity verification to tracking intelligence and carrier enrollment. The article also cites Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration warnings about broker and carrier identity theft, along with advice to check registration information and watch for suspicious contact changes. It recommends independent confirmation of high-risk changes, such as a new pickup contact, driver, equipment or payment instructions, made through a known channel rather than the incoming message. It also says a valid operating authority record does not by itself establish who is answering calls or receiving pickup instructions.</description></item><item><title>Texas Truck Wrecks in October 2026: 18-Wheeler and Commercial Vehicle Crash Statistics in Dallas, DFW and Statewide</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/texas-truck-wrecks-in-october-2026-18-wheeler-and-commercial-vehicle-c-50409fd411/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/texas-truck-wrecks-in-october-2026-18-wheeler-and-commercial-vehicle-c-50409fd411/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:40:33 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The Wooley Law Firm</description></item><item><title>Einride books $167M in contracted revenue, targets $250M</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/einride-books-167m-in-contracted-revenue-targets-250m-8573ce19e0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/einride-books-167m-in-contracted-revenue-targets-250m-8573ce19e0/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Freight Spending Jumps 32% as Volumes Barely Move</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/freight-spending-jumps-32-as-volumes-barely-move-978b3d13af/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/freight-spending-jumps-32-as-volumes-barely-move-978b3d13af/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:20:15 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>US rail traffic rises 7.3% as intermodal gains 10.7% in latest week</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/us-rail-traffic-rises-7-3-as-intermodal-gains-10-7-in-latest-week-9a93399240/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/us-rail-traffic-rises-7-3-as-intermodal-gains-10-7-in-latest-week-9a93399240/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:20:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Mayor Mamdani Moves To Curb Truck Impacts With Warehouse Regulations</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/mayor-mamdani-moves-to-curb-truck-impacts-with-warehouse-regulations-f7bba64d16/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/mayor-mamdani-moves-to-curb-truck-impacts-with-warehouse-regulations-f7bba64d16/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:10:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Streetsblog New York City</description></item><item><title>Bill to require bathroom access for truckers advances in Senate</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/bill-to-require-bathroom-access-for-truckers-advances-in-senate-062a68f0e2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/bill-to-require-bathroom-access-for-truckers-advances-in-senate-062a68f0e2/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:13:23 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Hours of Service (HOS) of Drivers; American Pyrotechnics Association (APA); Request To Include an Additional Member Company to Current APA HOS Exemptions</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/hours-of-service-hos-of-drivers-american-pyrotechnics-association-apa-9a344ffa94/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/hours-of-service-hos-of-drivers-american-pyrotechnics-association-apa-9a344ffa94/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Federal Register (FMCSA)</description></item><item><title>At least 14 charged in alleged $22.5 million California train cargo theft scheme</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/at-least-14-charged-in-alleged-22-5-million-california-train-cargo-the-c02dac559f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/at-least-14-charged-in-alleged-22-5-million-california-train-cargo-the-c02dac559f/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:12:55 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Federal prosecutors said at least 14 people have been charged over an alleged scheme that stole cargo worth $22.5 million from freight trains in Southern California. Prosecutors say the crew hit at least 36 freight trains between February 2024 and August 2026, cutting air hoses to force them to stop. Prosecutors identified Nathan Daniel Angel, 21, of East Los Angeles, as the alleged leader, operating with his father and two uncles. Officials said a Los Angeles-based sneaker resale business, which was not an authorized Nike reseller, bought stolen sneakers and generated more than $1 million for the crew. The defendants are presumed innocent, and the maximum penalties include five years for conspiracy and 10 years for each theft count.</description></item><item><title>14 Charged in SoCal Train Cargo Theft Ring, DOJ Says</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/14-charged-in-socal-train-cargo-theft-ring-doj-says-aab5c10b5d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/14-charged-in-socal-train-cargo-theft-ring-doj-says-aab5c10b5d/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:17:47 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Hoodline</description></item><item><title>14 Arrested in $22.5 Million Southern California Cargo Theft Ring</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/14-arrested-in-22-5-million-southern-california-cargo-theft-ring-1311c3d8ed/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/14-arrested-in-22-5-million-southern-california-cargo-theft-ring-1311c3d8ed/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Head Topics</description></item><item><title>Hydrogen-powered truck completes 1,046-km freight haul from Vancouver to Calgary</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/hydrogen-powered-truck-completes-1-046-km-freight-haul-from-vancouver-1056c5e2db/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/hydrogen-powered-truck-completes-1-046-km-freight-haul-from-vancouver-1056c5e2db/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:41:19 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Laredo Border Hours, Reefer Risks, Flexport AI: Week in Logistics</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/laredo-border-hours-reefer-risks-flexport-ai-week-in-logistics-37adab6927/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/laredo-border-hours-reefer-risks-flexport-ai-week-in-logistics-37adab6927/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:23:30 +0000</pubDate><category>Cross-Border</category><description>U.S. Customs and Border Protection and Mexico&#x27;s National Customs Agency, known as ANAM, extended a Saturday commercial truck processing pilot at Laredo&#x27;s World Trade Bridge, with the window now running until 7 p.m. The roundup says the extension adds three hours and lifts Saturday crossings by 400 to 500 trucks, while easing bottlenecks on Sunday and Monday. It also notes that cross-border volumes have reached record highs.</description></item><item><title>Truck drivers stranded in snow along interstate in California mountains</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truck-drivers-stranded-in-snow-along-interstate-in-california-mountain-8fab767786/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truck-drivers-stranded-in-snow-along-interstate-in-california-mountain-8fab767786/</guid><